From: Chris Trowbridge <chris.trowbridge@ezurio.com>
Date: Wed, 27 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] setup.cfg: exclude the test suite from the installed packages

setup.cfg declares "packages = find:" with no exclude list, and tests/
contains an __init__.py, so find: treats it as a shippable package and
installs it to site-packages/tests.

That name is not namespaced, so it collides with any other distribution
doing the same thing when both are installed into a shared prefix.

The test suite is only useful from a source checkout, so exclude it.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Yocto native integration adjustments]
Signed-off-by: Chris Trowbridge <chris.trowbridge@ezurio.com>
---
 setup.cfg | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/setup.cfg
+++ b/setup.cfg
@@ -26,6 +26,11 @@
 	importlib_metadata; python_version < "3.8"
 	t61codec >= 1.0.1, <2.0
 
+[options.packages.find]
+exclude =
+    tests
+    tests.*
+
 [options.extras_require]
 dev = 
 	Pygments
